  "summary_en": "The July 2025 White House AI Action Plan sets out three pillars, innovation, infrastructure and international diplomacy and security, to secure US AI dominance. It favors deregulation, open models, and adoption in government and defense. It also covers workforce, export controls, and security evaluations. It mentions robotics and drones only briefly, in the manufacturing section.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Remove regulatory barriers to AI, including federal rules and funding limits for states with burdensome AI regulation",
   "Revise the NIST AI RMF to drop references to misinformation, DEI and climate change",
   "Convene stakeholders on supply chain challenges for US robotics and drone manufacturing",
   "Establish regulatory sandboxes and an AI evaluations ecosystem led by NIST's CAISI",
   "Strengthen export controls and promote US AI standards internationally while countering Chinese influence"
